id: 17
hanzi: 钓
pinyin: diào
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Verb

meanings_summary:
  en: to fish with a hook and line; to angle for; to fish
  es: pescar con caña; pescar con anzuelo; buscar ardilosamente

senses[2]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Verb | Standard | to catch aquatic life using a hook, line, or rod | pescar peces u otros animales acuáticos con caña o anzuelo | 在海边钓鱼 (fish by the seashore)
  2 | Verb | Formal | to fish or angle for something indirectly (fame, praise, wealth) | buscar o pescar algo indirectamente como fama o favores | 沽名钓誉 (angle for fame and social praise)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 航行在太平洋中央时，全家人常常坐在船尾钓鱼，新鲜的金枪鱼成了餐桌上最美味的补给。 | Hángxíng zài Tàipíngyáng zhōngyāng shí, quán jiārén chángcháng zuò zài chuánwěi diàoyú, xīnxiān de jīnqiāngyú chéng le cānzhuō shàng zuì měiwèi de bǔjǐ. | While sailing through the middle of the Pacific, the family often angled off the stern, fresh tuna becoming their tastiest provision. | Durante la travesía por el Pacífico, la familia solía pescar con caña en la popa; el atún fresco se convirtió en su más sabroso manjar.
  #2 | 周末清晨，许多垂钓爱好者来到静谧的湖畔，在悠闲的等待中享受远离城市喧嚣的宁静时光。 | Zhōumò qīngchén, xǔduō chuídiào àihàozhě lái dào jìngmì de húpàn, zài yōuxián de děngdài zhōng xiǎngshòu yuǎnlí chéngshì xuānxiāo de níngjìng shíguāng. | On weekend mornings, angling enthusiasts gather by the tranquil lakeshore, savoring serene hours away from urban clamor through leisurely waiting. | En las mañanas de fin de semana, aficionados a la pesca acuden a la orilla del lago para disfrutar de un sosiego ajeno al ajetreo urbano mediante la espera paciente.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  钓鱼 | fish with a hook and line; go fishing
  钓竿 | fishing rod
  钓钩 | fishhook
  垂钓 | angle; fish with rod
  钓鱼岛 | Diaoyu Islands
  钓饵 | bait; lure

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  沽名钓誉 | gū míng diào yù | fish for fame and angle for compliments; seek unmerited recognition
  姜太公钓鱼 | Jiāng Tàigōng diào yú | Jiang Taigong fishing with a straight hook; willing victims bite of their own accord
  钓游之地 | diào yóu zhī dì | places where one fished and played in childhood; fondly remembered old haunts
  太公钓鱼 | tài gōng diào yú | Jiang Taigong fishing; willing fish stepping into the net willingly

character_decomposition[1]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  钓 | diào | fish with hook | pescar con anzuelo | 钅 | metal / gold | 钅 (metal fishhook) | 勺 (sháo phonetic / curved spoon or hook shape) | 8 | 左右结构 | Phono-semantic compound: a sharp metal barb (钅) shaped like a small curved scoop (勺) to catch fish. | A glittering metal barb (钅) curving like a tiny curved spoon (勺) dangling into deep water. | Un afilado anzuelo de metal brillante (钅) curvado como una diminuta cuchara (勺) para atrapar peces. | 51 | CPY | 釣

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: A curved metal hook (钅) scooping up (勺) swimming fish from the water allows you to fish (钓).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Un anzuelo de metal (钅) que recoge como una cuchara (勺) a los peces bajo el agua permite pescar (钓).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: The ancient legend of Jiang Ziya fishing with a straight, unbarbed hook (愿者上钩) made angling a profound Chinese philosophical metaphor for waiting patiently for destiny rather than forcing outcomes.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Falling 4th tone: diào (51). Deliver a clean, firm downward pitch contour from high to low.

traps_and_cognates:
  look_alikes[4]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,distinction_note}:
    钓 | diào | fish with hook | Has 钅 on the left and 勺 on the right
    钩 | gōu | hook; barb | Has 钅 on the left and 勾 on the right
    钓 | diào | fish with hook | Has 钅 and 勺 (with inner dot)
    的 | de / dì | possessive particle; target | Has 白 on the left with 勺
  etymological_cognates[4]{character,pinyin,gloss_en}:
    钓具 | diào jù | fishing tackle; fishing gear
    钓手 | diào shǒu | angler; fisherman
    垂钓 | chuí diào | go angling; gentle fishing
    海钓 | hǎi diào | sea fishing; offshore angling

semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 钓 refers specifically to catching aquatic creatures using a hook and line or metaphorically luring someone.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 钓 vs. 捕 | bǔ | 钓 is recreational or small-scale angling using hooks, lines, and bait, whereas 捕 involves active catching, netting, trapping, or arresting (捕鱼, 捕捞, 捕捉).
    2 | 钓 vs. 捞 | lāo | 钓 relies on enticing fish with bait on a hook, while 捞 means directly scooping up or dredging items from underwater using nets or hands.
    3 | 钓 vs. 捉 | zhuō | 钓 is restricted to line fishing or covert luring, while 捉 describes physically seizing or grasping by hand (捉贼, 捉迷藏).

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 坐在平静的船舷边钓鱼，与其说是在等待水下的收获，不如说是在与自己的心灵对话。浮漂在微波间起伏，所有的焦虑与急躁都在无声的守候中渐渐平息。懂得等待的人，才能真正领会大自然赋予的静谧与从容。 | Zuò zài píngjìng de chuánxián biān diàoyú, yǔqí shuō shì zài děngdài shuǐxià de shōuhuò, bùrú shuō shì zài yǔ zìjǐ de xīnlíng duìhuà. Fúpiāo zài wēibō jiān qǐfú, suǒyǒu de jiāolǜ yǔ jízào dōu zài wúshēng de shǒuhòu zhōng jiànjiàn píngxī. Dǒngde děngdài de rén, cáinéng zhēnzhèng lǐnghuì dàzìrán fùyǔ de jìngmì yǔ cóngròng. | Angling beside a tranquil gunwale is less about awaiting a catch than dialoguing with one's soul. As the bobber bobs among ripples, anxieties quiet in the vigil. Only those versed in waiting truly grasp nature's stillness and grace. | Sentarse a pescar junto a la borda tranquila es más un coloquio íntimo con el alma que el anhelo de una presa. El flotador baila en el agua y las inquietudes se apaciguan en la espera. Quien domina la paciencia saborea el sosiego que la naturaleza brinda.
  #2 | 生态保护政策推动了水域治理转型，规范化的休闲垂钓逐渐成为生态渔业的新形态。通过限定钓具规格与渔获放生标准，水生系统得以有效休养生息，实现了生态修复与休闲生活的有机融合。 | Shēngtài bǎohù zhèngcè tuīdòng le shuǐyù zhìlǐ zhuǎnxíng, guīfànhuà de xiūxián chuídiào zhújiàn chéngwéi shēngtài yúyè de xīn xíngtài. Tōngguò xiàndìng diàojù guīgé yǔ yúhuò fàngshēng biāozhǔn, shuǐshēng xìtǒng déyǐ yǒuxiào xiūyǎngxēngxī, shíxiàn le shēngtài xiūfù yǔ xiūxián shēnghuó de yǒujī rónghé. | Conservation policies have transformed aquatic governance, establishing regulated recreational angling as a sustainable model. Setting tackle limits and catch-and-release rules lets aquatic biomes recover while harmonizing ecology with leisure. | Las políticas ambientales han transformado la gestión de las aguas, haciendo de la pesca deportiva un modelo sostenible. Fijar normas de aparejos y captura y suelta permite regenerar la fauna acuática aunando ecología y recreo.
